working branch contains only specifications and that generated code lives elsewhere at generation-merged tags. The code status shows \"not started\" for the format use case, yet the source code is provided in the project context. I think the distinction is that the `source_code` section contains reference implementations or templates, but I need to understand what the actual task is asking me to generate on this branch.\n\nThe repository already has several format files like `color.go`, `columns.go`, and `size.go` with their tests, but `table.go` is missing. The task description indicates I need to create `pkg/format/table.go` for column alignment in tabular output. I need to check the PRD to understand the canonical type names for the format package, since the task requires naming files after their primary exported types rather than generic names like `table.go`. The existing `columns.go` file is already in the repository, so I should verify whether it needs renaming or if `table.go` is meant to be something different entirely based on what the PRD specifies. I need to read the PRD file since it's listed in the repository but not included in the project context, and the constraints allow me to read files that aren't already provided. Let me also check what use case files are available to understand the full scope of requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38085,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38085},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d47fb82-0e76-4eac-81b0-180fd01d344c","uuid":"e44c3708-86b5-4236-a874-8ab34c4f5939"}
